Incremental fixes on top of 39751_3.diff (tu/kgsl: timeline-based sync).
Apply to a tree that already has 39751_3.diff applied:

    git apply --check tu-kgsl-timeline-improvements.patch && git apply tu-kgsl-timeline-improvements.patch

 * binary sync: import of fd == -1 (already signaled) no longer hands -1 to the kernel as a fence syncpoint
 * binary sync: CPU waits on an imported sync file are handled instead of waiting forever on the unsignaled timeline
 * submit: queue timeline is only waited on by empty submits (no per-submit stall on the previous submit's retirement)
 * submit: fast path for empty submits whose waits are already signaled (the half the comments describe but the diff lacked)
 * submit: no SYNC flag / zero-count syncpoint list on bind submits without waits
 * profiling: embed the kgsl_command_object instead of vk_alloc'ing it per traced submit (it was never freed)
 * load: TU_KGSL_NO_TIMELINE=1 forces the old syncobj implementation
 * misc: wait_count == 0 guard in timeline wait_many, ret/timestamp initialised, queue->fence updated for empty submits

